it's so clear that the republicans they  have a strategy and they're  executing their strategy it is  suppressing the votes  of voters of color and young people who  turned out for joe biden  and flipped georgia and arizona and who  according to data less likely to vote  for republicans so  what's the democrat strategy  look we believe in fighting fair and  having laws in place that make it easier  for people to vote right syria that's  the whole point of a democracy  not to think well the only way i can win  is if i can  suppress in ways that are inconsistent  with the core values of our democracy  your right to vote and you're right in a  very diabolical way  particularly across the south we are  seeing increasing numbers of legislators  who did not like the outcome of the  election which was fair and square  don't listen to me listen to president  trump's former attorney general who said  it was all nonsense to think that the  election wasn't on the up and up  so they say okay well if we can't win  fair and square let's see what we can do  to suppress the vote there are 48 states  where republicans in their legislatures  are trying to make it harder to vote  in the absence of vote fraud and it is  clearly an intent to discourage black  and brown  people from being able to vote and young  people too for that matter  and the only thing that stands in the  way of that happening  is us the american people which is why  we have to speak out loud and clearly on  this issue  voting rights was a critical issue going  back to 2013 when the shelby decision  happened  and that was during the obama  administration can you talk about the  ways attorney general eric holder who  was included in that conversation  the ways a.g holder and your  administration in particular work to  protect voting rights because  as soon as that shelby decision was  handed down the doj  they went to work what did they do  well we tried very hard state by state  to try to protect  um the the ability for local uh  folks who are responsible for the  elections to have fair and open  elections  and that was much harder after shelby  shelby  required the burden of proof to be on  them to say okay we are  operating a fair election it shifted  when that protection was gutted from the  voting rights act and we tried  to get congress the republicans in  congress to be specific  to reauthorize it because what the  supreme court said is  we're not going to uphold it but go back  to congress that's your remedy  and get them to do so and the fact that  since that time  not only have the republicans in  congress not move forward with a  reauthorization  but as i said state by state they have  been trying to pass laws to suppress the  vote and on top of that  they are giving voice to the nonsense  they're trying to bamboozle the american  people  into thinking that there was something  unfair  about the last election and that is  harmful for  to our democracy no matter who's in  office  we hold ourselves out selena around the  world  as a country that has a strong democracy  and so if we are supporting  insurrections and saying that they're  just like your average tour  of the capital if we are condoning those  who  question the election those who  criticize the vice president of the  united states for certifying the  election  something he just spoke out and said he  had no choice to do then we are in  trouble and so yes during president  obama's time in office  eric holder was a leader in this effort  um trying to ensure that he protected  the rights  of citizens and i'm heartened to see  that merrick garner garland  uh the attorney general today is has  filed a lawsuit  against the state of georgia and saying  that the laws that they passed  are unconstitutional and that's what we  are going to have to do state by state  by state  but i also want to just say let's just  not leave it to the attorney generals  to fight on our behalf we have to add  our voices to the equation and we have  to vote  out of office people who are doing these  dastardly deeds  it feels like and the word bamboozled is  under underutilized frankly i think um  it is a very good word and i feel like  in a lot of ways  you know when you when you put it that  way it just  it it's so applicable here because we  all want a democracy like i don't care  what side of the political  aisle you're on or what you care about  in terms of tax cuts like what the  tax rate you prefer is that's not the  point the point is is that  you want it to be fair for everybody and  so many  these laws are going into place and  they're already in place so at this  point it's a it's a little bit about  mitigating the damage  what are some of the ways that can be  done um is it is it just  the voters at home calling congress  until  they finally pick up um to ensure that  there's federal legislation as soon as  possible or are there other things that  biden can do well as we spoke his  attorney general  on his own independently is challenging  laws  uh on the basis of them being  unconstitutional  inconsistent with the voting rights act  uh those laws that are suppressing the  vote  look just take georgia they're making it  harder for people to vote  absentee they're they're saying it's a  it's a crime if you take  food or drinks to somebody who's  standing in line come on now  we're standing in line you don't think  that somebody should be able to bring us  food or water particularly  in a state where we know that there are  long lines and people have to wait for  hours to vote  and so we need our justice department  doing exactly what attorney general  merrick garland is doing  we need to have people who are voting  and showing up at the polls  in record numbers and so if i'm  out there and i'm hearing this story  that somebody's trying to  bamboozle me and tell me that the  election is unfair and i  know that that's not true and i know  that they're trying to suppress my vote  i'm going to stand in line and be even  more determined to vote  i'm going to show up and make sure my  vote counts because  i know that i stand on the shoulders of  people who fought and  sacrificed greatly for me to have that  right to vote  i'm not going to let any legislator take  it away from me so we should be  outraged and we should be more  determined than ever no matter what  obstacles they put in our way  to show up and vote and we need to make  sure that we have an administration  which we are fortunate enough to have  right now  with president biden and his attorney  general who are going to fight those  laws state by state by state  if they deem them to be unconstitutional  as many of them are  i want to turn now to the insurrection  on january 6  president obama spoke at an event today  about  that the attack on the capital and the  potential for a repeat  so let's take a listen  the guard rails i thought were in place  around  many of our democratic institutions uh  really depend on the two parties  agreeing to those ground rules those  guard rails and that one of them right  now  doesn't seem as committed to him  as in previous generations that worries  me  uh and i think we should all be worried  i mean i think there's sort of  proverbial guardrails and real  guardrails that  we all were surprised uh weren't as firm  as we thought  at this rate how much democracy is at  risk  how much is democracy at risks oh sorry  julian i think i think we are at a  precipice here  when the sitting president of the united  states  tells people that the election was  unfair even though his own  administration  from the fbi to homeland security to the  justice department tells him that's not  true  yet he perpetuates this farce that it  was a  that it was an election that was stolen  from him when he tells his supporters  that they should take to the streets  and go and fight to defend his  presidency which he lost  and they respond in kind  and stormed the capital and then  the republicans decide that we shouldn't  investigate what happened and find  out who was behind it and we see  evidence that  some of them were complicit in that  attack and the very ones who said well  it was nothing other than an ordinary  tour we see photographs of them  barricaded in trying to protect  themselves  from this onslaught if that scene  happened in any other country around the  world  the united states would be the first to  point at finger and say  that is a threat to democracy and the  republicans who condone that  have to be held accountable and so we  need to get to the facts we have to have  transparency with the american people  and those guard rails are what protects  our democracy  and so if we let them just fall by the  wayside  then who are we who are we  it's a good question that i think folks  should uh  marinate on a little bit valerie jarrett  thank you as always for taking the time  to join me today and please stay safe  hi i'm zerlina maxwell thanks for  checking out our channel on youtube  you can see more from zerlina by  clicking any of the videos on this  screen  and make sure you subscribe below to  stay up to date on the day's biggest  stories  thanks for watching

